The legal texts are Jersey legislation, as published by the Jersey Legal Information Board on Jersey Law
(www.jerseylaw.je): the current official consolidations and the Laws as enacted. The States Assembly holds the
copyright in Jersey legislation (Intellectual Property (Unregistered Rights) (Jersey) Law 2011, Articles 185 and 186).
The Greffier of the States offers the legislation published on the current laws, laws as enacted and pending laws
pages for use and re-use under the Open States Assembly Licence (OSAL-J) v.1
(https://www.jerseylaw.je/Pages/copyright.aspx). Source: Jersey Law, jerseylaw.je, (c) States Assembly.

Orders in Council and other UK instruments published on jerseylaw.je are Crown copyright, re-used under the Open
Government Licence v3.0 (https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/).

The list of page addresses came from the Internet Archive's Wayback Machine CDX index (archive.org); no text was
taken from it.

Lexifina's own work in this repository (its arrangement, tables, commit messages and tools) is dedicated to the
public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). This repository is not
legal advice and not an official publication.
